{"name":"Garden Party","hex":"#e3a4b8","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"garden party","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A party held on a lawn or in a park, usually more formal than a picnic or barbecue."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden_party"}],"entries":[{"title":"Garden Party (2008 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Garden Party is a 2008 American drama film directed by Jason Freeland, and starring Vinessa Shaw and Willa Holland. A low-budget independent film, it marked Jennifer Lawrence's film debut."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d6/Garden_party_post.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden_Party_(2008_film)","wikidata":"Q2272447"},{"title":"Garden Party (Rick Nelson song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Garden Party\" is a 1972 song written by Rick Nelson and recorded by him and the Stone Canyon Band for the album Garden Party. The song tells the story of Nelson being booed at a concert at Madison Square Garden. It was Nelson's last top 40 hit, reaching No. 6 on the U.S. Billboard pop chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/17/Garden_Party_-_Rick_Nelson_and_The_Stone_Canyon_Band.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden_Party_(Rick_Nelson_song)","wikidata":"Q3079925"},{"title":"Party","blocks":[{"text":"A party is a gathering of people who have been invited by a host for the purposes of socializing, conversation, recreation, or as part of a festival or other commemoration or celebration of a special occasion. A party will often feature food and beverages, and generally conversation, music, dancing, or other forms of entertainment."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Hip%2C_Hip%2C_Hurrah%21_Artists%E2%80%99_Party%2C_Skagen_%28Peder_Severin_Kr%C3%B8yer%29_-_Gothenburg_Museum_o